    "result": "I implemented `plan_extraction` in `solution.py` and left the `UnsafePathError` class and the signature unchanged. Each member is checked for NUL characters, absolute paths, and Windows drive prefixes. Both `/` and `\\` are treated as separators, and empty and `.` segments are dropped. A `..` that would climb above the destination raises, and a member that normalises to nothing raises too. Directory entries (names ending in a separator) are validated but left out of the result. File targets are built as `base + \"/\" + normalised`, where `base` is `dest` with trailing slashes stripped, so `\"/\"` gives `/name`. Duplicate targets are detected by casefolded comparison and raise. Any unsafe member raises before the function returns, so no partial plan comes back. I did not run or test the code, since shell access was not available.",
